00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
This is the Peg-la-Don, and you are listening to KCPR, San Luis Obispo.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
My name is Peggy Kuzimech.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:12.000
I'm a first-year student from Sacramento, California, and my major is journalism.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:20.500
On campus, I am involved in KCPR, which is the on-campus radio station, which kinda coincides with my journalism major.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
I'm also involved with the Field Studies Club and the sorority Delta Gamma.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.500
Being in KCPR has been a big part of my school year already as a first-year.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:43.500
It just is a really good community where everyone can kind of express themselves, which is my favorite part. So being in KCPR has really given me a lot of new friends and a place where I can really be myself.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.500
I would give the advice to first-year students that are trying to find their place: just go to meetings.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:56.000
If anything is really interesting to you, go out there because college is different in the sense that no one's gonna drag you to meetings.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:02.000
It's kinda you have to take the first step and get out there, and it may be hard and daunting to make friends.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.000
But it's so worth it in the end. So I'd say just take that first step.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.000
It's gonna be awkward at first, but you'll get to know people, and it'll be a good time.